module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Crystalline.SmallSite.SituationRestrict
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Crystalline.SmallSite.SmoothLiftingComparison
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Crystalline.SmallSite.SmoothLiftingZariskiRestriction

/-!
# Restricting the situation of [Stacks, Tag 07MW] to an open of `X`

Let `T` be the situation of Remark [Stacks, Tag 07MW] over a global crystalline situation
`(p, (S, I, γ), X)` (`...SmallSite.Situation07MW`): `S` affine, `p` nilpotent in `Γ(S, 𝒪_S)`, a
smooth `Y ⟶ S` and a cartesian square exhibiting `X` as `Y ×_S S₀`.  The object `(X, Y, γ)` of
`Cris(X/S)` it defines (`Situation07MW.crystallineThickening`) has the homeomorphism `X ≅ Y` as its
immersion, so an open `W` of `X` corresponds to the open `V = h⁻¹(W)` of `Y`
(`...SmallSite.CrystallineThickening.ambientToXPreimage`), and `W = X ×_Y V`.

This file restricts the situation to `W`.  The restricted global crystalline situation is
`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.restrict S ⊤ W _`, with base `S|_⊤ ≅ S` and thickened
space `W`, and on it

* `Situation07MW.restrictToOpen` is again a situation of [Stacks, Tag 07MW]: its smooth lifting is
  `V`, with structure morphism `V ↪ Y ⟶ S ≅ S|_⊤`, and `W ⟶ V` is the restriction of `X ⟶ Y`; the
  square is cartesian because it is the restriction of the given one over the open `V` of `Y`;
* `Situation07MW.restrictToOpenCrystallineThickeningIso` identifies the object `(W, V, γ)` it
  defines, carried back to `Cris(X/S)` by `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.smallExtend`,
  with the restriction `(X, Y, γ)|_V` of the object of the whole situation.

The only point of substance in the last identification is that the two divided power structures
on the ideal of `W` in `V` agree: one is the extension of `γ` along `Γ(S, 𝒪_S) ⟶ Γ(V, 𝒪_V)` made
for the restricted situation, the other the restriction to `V` of the extension made on `Y`.  On
every affine open the ideal is generated by the image of `I`, and both structures make the map
from `(Γ(S, 𝒪_S), I, γ)` a divided power morphism, so they agree by the uniqueness of extensions
of divided powers, [Stacks, Tag 07H1]; in the form used here this is
`DividedPowers.IsDPMorphism.of_comp`, packaged as
`Crystalline.DividedPowerScheme.isDPMorphism_app_of_ideal_map`.

## Main definitions

Except for the two general lemmas on divided power schemes at the start, everything lives in the
namespace `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite.Situation07MW`.

* `liftingOpen` — the open `V = h⁻¹(W)` of `Y`.
* `restrictToOpen` — the situation of [Stacks, Tag 07MW] restricted to `W`.
* `restrictToOpenCrystallineThickeningIso` — the object of the restricted situation, carried to
  `Cris(X/S)`, is the restriction of the object of the whole situation to `V`.

## Main results

* `Crystalline.DividedPowerScheme.isDPMorphism_app_of_ideal_map` — a morphism of schemes over a
  common divided power base respects the divided powers when the ideal of its target is generated,
  on affine opens, by the ideal of the base.
* `le_sourceToBase_preimage_top` — every open of `X` lies over `⊤`, so that the restricted
  situation is defined.
* `isAffine_restrict_X` and `isAffine_restrictToOpen_Y` — when `V` is affine, so are the thickened
  space and the smooth lifting of the restricted situation (`W ⟶ V` being a closed immersion).

## What is and is not proved

Everything stated is proved.  No tag attribute is placed: this is bookkeeping towards
[Stacks, Tag 07MW] part (3), not a statement of the source.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07MW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07MW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07H1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07H1)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry Opposite
open scoped AlgebraicGeometry

universe u

noncomputable section

namespace Crystalline.DividedPowerScheme

/-! ### Comparing divided power structures through a common base -/

/-- The map of rings from the global sections of a divided power scheme `B` to the sections over
an open `U` of a divided power scheme mapping to it is a divided power morphism. -/
theorem isDPMorphism_map_comp_appTop {B D : DividedPowerScheme.{u}} (ψ : D ⟶ B)
    (U : D.scheme.Opens) :
    DividedPowers.IsDPMorphism (B.dividedPowers.dividedPowers (op ⊤))
      (D.dividedPowers.dividedPowers (op U))
      ((D.scheme.presheaf.map (homOfLE (show U ≤ ⊤ from le_top)).op).hom.comp
        ψ.hom.appTop.hom) :=
  DividedPowers.IsDPMorphism.comp (D.dividedPowers.dividedPowers (op U))
    (D.dividedPowers.naturality (homOfLE (show U ≤ ψ.hom ⁻¹ᵁ ⊤ from le_top)).op)
    (ψ.compatible ⊤)

/-- **Two divided power schemes over a common base whose ideals are generated by the ideal of the
base are compared by any morphism over the base.**  Let `ψ₁ : D₁ ⟶ B` and `ψ₂ : D₂ ⟶ B` be
morphisms of divided power schemes and `φ : D₂ ⟶ D₁` a morphism of the underlying schemes over
`B`.  If on every affine open of `D₁` the divided power ideal is generated by the image of the
divided power ideal of `B` over `⊤`, then `φ` is compatible with the divided powers.

On affine opens this is the uniqueness of extensions of divided powers along a ring map,
[Stacks, Tag 07H1], in the form `DividedPowers.IsDPMorphism.of_comp`; it then holds on every open
by `Crystalline.DividedPowerScheme.isDPMorphism_app_of_affine`. -/
theorem isDPMorphism_app_of_ideal_map {B D₁ D₂ : DividedPowerScheme.{u}} (ψ₁ : D₁ ⟶ B)
    (ψ₂ : D₂ ⟶ B) (φ : D₂.scheme ⟶ D₁.scheme) (hφ : φ ≫ ψ₁.hom = ψ₂.hom)
    (hI : ∀ U : D₁.scheme.affineOpens,
      Ideal.map ((D₁.scheme.presheaf.map (homOfLE (show U.1 ≤ ⊤ from le_top)).op).hom.comp
        ψ₁.hom.appTop.hom) (B.ideal.obj (op ⊤)) = D₁.ideal.obj (op U.1))
    (U : D₁.scheme.Opens) :
    DividedPowers.IsDPMorphism (D₁.dividedPowers.dividedPowers (op U))
      (D₂.dividedPowers.dividedPowers (op (φ ⁻¹ᵁ U))) (φ.app U).hom := by
  refine DividedPowerScheme.isDPMorphism_app_of_affine D₂ D₁ φ (fun V W h => ?_) U
  refine DividedPowers.IsDPMorphism.of_comp _ _ _
    ((D₁.scheme.presheaf.map (homOfLE (show V.1 ≤ ⊤ from le_top)).op).hom.comp
      ψ₁.hom.appTop.hom) (φ.appLE V.1 W.1 h).hom (hI V).symm
    (isDPMorphism_map_comp_appTop ψ₁ V.1) ?_
  have key : ψ₁.hom.appTop ≫ D₁.scheme.presheaf.map (homOfLE (show V.1 ≤ ⊤ from le_top)).op ≫
      φ.appLE V.1 W.1 h =
        ψ₂.hom.appTop ≫ D₂.scheme.presheaf.map (homOfLE (show W.1 ≤ ⊤ from le_top)).op := by
    rw [Scheme.Hom.map_appLE, ← hφ, Scheme.Hom.comp_appTop]
    simp [Scheme.Hom.appLE]
  have e := congrArg CommRingCat.Hom.hom key
  simp only [CommRingCat.hom_comp] at e
  rw [← RingHom.comp_assoc, e]
  exact isDPMorphism_map_comp_appTop ψ₂ W.1

end Crystalline.DividedPowerScheme

namespace Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite.Situation07MW

variable {S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}} (T : Situation07MW S) (W : S.X.Opens)

/-! ### The restricted situation -/

/-- **Every open of `X` lies over the whole base**, so that the situation restricted to the base
`S|_⊤` and the open `W` of `X` is defined. -/
theorem le_sourceToBase_preimage_top : W ≤ sourceToBase S ⁻¹ᵁ ⊤ := by
  simp

/-- **The open `V = h⁻¹(W)` of the smooth lifting `Y` attached to an open `W` of `X`**, the
preimage of `W` under the inverse `h : Y ⟶ X` of the homeomorphism `X ≅ Y`. -/
abbrev liftingOpen : T.Y.Opens :=
  CrystallineThickening.ambientToXPreimage T.crystallineThickening W

/-- **`W = X ×_Y V`**: the preimage of `V = h⁻¹(W)` under `X ⟶ Y` is `W`. -/
theorem toY_preimage_liftingOpen : T.toY ⁻¹ᵁ T.liftingOpen W = W :=
  CrystallineThickening.immersion_preimage_ambientToXPreimage T.crystallineThickening W

/-- The isomorphism `S|_⊤ ≅ S` of the underlying schemes, `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.topIso`, with
its source named as the underlying scheme of the divided power scheme `S|_⊤`. -/
def baseTopIso : (S.S.restrict ⊤).scheme ≅ S.S.scheme :=
  S.S.scheme.topIso

/-- The isomorphism `S|_⊤ ≅ S` is the restriction morphism `S|_⊤ ⟶ S`. -/
@[simp]
theorem baseTopIso_hom : (baseTopIso (S := S)).hom = (S.S.restrictι ⊤).hom :=
  rfl

/-- The structure morphism `V ↪ Y ⟶ S ≅ S|_⊤` of the restricted smooth lifting. -/
def restrictToBase : (T.liftingOpen W).toScheme ⟶ (S.S.restrict ⊤).scheme :=
  (T.liftingOpen W).ι ≫ T.toBase ≫ (baseTopIso (S := S)).inv

/-- The structure morphism of the restricted smooth lifting, followed by `S|_⊤ ⟶ S`, is
`V ↪ Y ⟶ S`. -/
@[reassoc (attr := simp)]
theorem restrictToBase_restrictι :
    T.restrictToBase W ≫ (S.S.restrictι ⊤).hom = (T.liftingOpen W).ι ≫ T.toBase := by
  rw [restrictToBase, Category.assoc, Category.assoc, ← baseTopIso_hom, Iso.inv_hom_id,
    Category.comp_id]

/-- The map `W ⟶ V`, the restriction of `X ⟶ Y`. -/
def restrictToY : W.toScheme ⟶ (T.liftingOpen W).toScheme :=
  IsOpenImmersion.lift (T.liftingOpen W).ι (W.ι ≫ T.toY) (by
    rintro _ ⟨x, rfl⟩
    rw [Scheme.Opens.range_ι]
    have hx : W.ι x ∈ T.toY ⁻¹ᵁ T.liftingOpen W := by
      rw [toY_preimage_liftingOpen]
      exact x.2
    exact hx)

/-- The map `W ⟶ V` followed by `V ↪ Y` is `W ↪ X ⟶ Y`. -/
@[reassoc (attr := simp)]
theorem restrictToY_ι : T.restrictToY W ≫ (T.liftingOpen W).ι = W.ι ≫ T.toY :=
  IsOpenImmersion.lift_fac _ _ _

/-- **The square on `W`, `V`, `X` and `Y` is cartesian**, `V` being an open of `Y` whose preimage
in `X` is `W`. -/
theorem isPullback_restrictToY :
    IsPullback (T.restrictToY W) W.ι (T.liftingOpen W).ι T.toY :=
  IsOpenImmersion.isPullback _ _ _ _ (T.restrictToY_ι W).symm (by
    rw [Scheme.Opens.opensRange_ι, Scheme.Opens.opensRange_ι]
    exact T.toY_preimage_liftingOpen W)

/-- The identification of the closed fibre of `S` with the closed fibre of `S|_⊤`. -/
def closedFiberTopIso :
    DividedPowerScheme.closedFiber S.S ≅ DividedPowerScheme.closedFiber (S.S.restrict ⊤) :=
  (DividedPowerScheme.closedFiber S.S).topIso.symm ≪≫
    (DividedPowerScheme.closedFiber S.S).isoOfEq
      (by simp : (⊤ : (DividedPowerScheme.closedFiber S.S).Opens) =
        DividedPowerScheme.closedFiberι S.S ⁻¹ᵁ ⊤) ≪≫
    (DividedPowerScheme.restrictClosedFiberIso S.S ⊤).symm

/-- **The cartesian square of the restricted situation**: `W = V ×_{S|_⊤} (S|_⊤)₀`.  It is the
square of `T` restricted over the open `V` of `Y` (`isPullback_restrictToY`, pasted with
`T.cartesian`), read through `S|_⊤ ≅ S` and the identification of the closed fibres. -/
theorem isPullback_restrict :
    IsPullback (T.restrictToY W)
      (restrictToClosedFiberAux S ⊤ W (le_sourceToBase_preimage_top W) ≫
        (DividedPowerScheme.restrictClosedFiberIso S.S ⊤).inv)
      (T.restrictToBase W) (DividedPowerScheme.closedFiberι (S.S.restrict ⊤)) := by
  refine ((T.isPullback_restrictToY W).paste_vert T.cartesian).of_iso (Iso.refl _) (Iso.refl _)
    (closedFiberTopIso (S := S)) (baseTopIso (S := S)).symm (by simp) ?_
    (by simp only [Iso.refl_hom, Category.id_comp, Category.assoc, restrictToBase]; rfl) ?_
  · have h1 : W.ι ≫ S.toClosedFiber ≫ (DividedPowerScheme.closedFiber S.S).topIso.inv ≫
        ((DividedPowerScheme.closedFiber S.S).isoOfEq
          (by simp : (⊤ : (DividedPowerScheme.closedFiber S.S).Opens) =
            DividedPowerScheme.closedFiberι S.S ⁻¹ᵁ ⊤)).hom =
          restrictToClosedFiberAux S ⊤ W (le_sourceToBase_preimage_top W) := by
      rw [← cancel_mono (DividedPowerScheme.closedFiberι S.S ⁻¹ᵁ ⊤).ι,
        restrictToClosedFiberAux_ι]
      simp
    simp only [closedFiberTopIso, Iso.trans_hom, Iso.symm_hom, Iso.refl_hom, Category.id_comp,
      Category.assoc]
    rw [← h1]
    simp only [Category.assoc]
  · refine (cancel_mono (baseTopIso (S := S)).hom).mp ?_
    simp only [Iso.symm_hom, Category.assoc, baseTopIso_hom,
      ← DividedPowerScheme.closedFiberMap_comp_closedFiberι, closedFiberTopIso, Iso.trans_hom,
      DividedPowerScheme.restrictClosedFiberIso_inv_closedFiberMap_assoc,
      Scheme.isoOfEq_hom_ι_assoc, Scheme.toIso_inv_ι_assoc]
    rw [← baseTopIso_hom, Iso.inv_hom_id, Category.comp_id]

/-- **The situation of [Stacks, Tag 07MW] restricted to an open `W` of `X`.**  The base is
`S|_⊤ ≅ S`, still affine with `p` nilpotent; the smooth lifting is the open `V = h⁻¹(W)` of `Y`,
with structure morphism `V ↪ Y ⟶ S ≅ S|_⊤`, smooth as a composite of an open immersion, a smooth
morphism and an isomorphism; the map `W ⟶ V` is the restriction of `X ⟶ Y`, and the square is the
restriction of the cartesian square of `T` (`isPullback_restrict`). -/
def restrictToOpen : Situation07MW (restrict S ⊤ W (le_sourceToBase_preimage_top W)) where
  isAffine :=
    have := T.isAffine
    isAffineOpen_top S.S.scheme
  prime_nilpotent := by
    have h := T.prime_nilpotent.map ((⊤ : S.S.scheme.Opens).ι.appTop.hom)
    rw [map_natCast] at h
    exact h
  Y := (T.liftingOpen W).toScheme
  toBase := T.restrictToBase W
  isSmooth := by
    have := T.isSmooth
    have : Smooth (T.toBase ≫ (baseTopIso (S := S)).inv) := inferInstance
    exact inferInstanceAs (Smooth ((T.liftingOpen W).ι ≫ T.toBase ≫ (baseTopIso (S := S)).inv))
  toY := T.restrictToY W
  cartesian := T.isPullback_restrict W

/-- The smooth lifting of the restricted situation is the open `V` of `Y`. -/
@[simp]
theorem restrictToOpen_Y : (T.restrictToOpen W).Y = (T.liftingOpen W).toScheme := rfl

/-- The structure morphism of the restricted situation, by definition. -/
@[simp]
theorem restrictToOpen_toBase : (T.restrictToOpen W).toBase = T.restrictToBase W := rfl

/-- The map `W ⟶ V` of the restricted situation, by definition. -/
@[simp]
theorem restrictToOpen_toY : (T.restrictToOpen W).toY = T.restrictToY W := rfl

/-- The map `W ⟶ V` is a closed immersion, being the base change of `(S|_⊤)₀ ↪ S|_⊤`. -/
instance isClosedImmersion_restrictToY : IsClosedImmersion (T.restrictToY W) :=
  (isThickening_toY (restrict S ⊤ W (le_sourceToBase_preimage_top W))
    (T.restrictToOpen W).prime_nilpotent (T.restrictToOpen W).Y (T.restrictToOpen W).toBase
    (T.restrictToOpen W).toY (T.restrictToOpen W).cartesian).1

/-- **If `V` is affine, so is `W`**: `W ⟶ V` is a closed immersion. -/
theorem isAffine_restrict_X (hV : IsAffineOpen (T.liftingOpen W)) :
    IsAffine (restrict S ⊤ W (le_sourceToBase_preimage_top W)).X :=
  have : IsAffine (T.liftingOpen W).toScheme := hV
  show IsAffine W.toScheme from isAffine_of_isAffineHom (T.restrictToY W)

/-- **If `V` is affine, so is the smooth lifting of the restricted situation**, which is `V`. -/
theorem isAffine_restrictToOpen_Y (hV : IsAffineOpen (T.liftingOpen W)) :
    IsAffine (T.restrictToOpen W).Y :=
  hV

/-! ### The object of the restricted situation in `Cris(X/S)` -/

/-- The object `(W, V, γ)` of the restricted situation, carried back to `Cris(X/S)`. -/
abbrev extendedObject : CrystallineThickening S :=
  (smallExtend S ⊤ W (le_sourceToBase_preimage_top W)).obj
    (T.restrictToOpen W).crystallineThickening

/-- The restriction `(X, Y, γ)|_V` of the object of the whole situation. -/
abbrev restrictedObject : CrystallineThickening S :=
  T.crystallineThickening.restrictOpen (T.liftingOpen W)

/-- The structure morphisms to `S` of the two objects agree on underlying schemes: both are
`V ↪ Y ⟶ S`. -/
theorem extendedObject_toBase_hom :
    (T.extendedObject W).obj.toBase.hom = (T.restrictedObject W).obj.toBase.hom :=
  T.restrictToBase_restrictι W

/-- The identification of the thickened schemes `W` and `X ×_Y V` of the two objects. -/
def sourceIso : W.toScheme ≅ (T.toY ⁻¹ᵁ T.liftingOpen W).toScheme :=
  S.X.isoOfEq (T.toY_preimage_liftingOpen W).symm

/-- The map `W ⟶ V` is the restriction `X ×_Y V ⟶ V` of `X ⟶ Y`, through `sourceIso`. -/
theorem restrictToY_eq :
    T.restrictToY W = (T.sourceIso W).hom ≫ (T.toY ∣_ T.liftingOpen W) := by
  rw [← cancel_mono (T.liftingOpen W).ι, restrictToY_ι, Category.assoc, morphismRestrict_ι,
    sourceIso, Scheme.isoOfEq_hom_ι_assoc]

/-- **The two objects have the same divided power ideal on every affine open of `V`**: both are
the ideal of `W` in `V`. -/
theorem ideal_obj_extendedObject (U : (T.liftingOpen W).toScheme.affineOpens) :
    (T.extendedObject W).obj.thickening.target.ideal.obj (op U.1) =
      (T.restrictedObject W).obj.thickening.target.ideal.obj (op U.1) :=
  ((T.extendedObject W).obj.thickening.ideal_eq_ker U).trans <|
    (congrArg (fun f => Scheme.Hom.ker f |>.ideal U) (T.restrictToY_eq W)).trans <| by
      rw [Scheme.Hom.ker_comp_of_isIso]
      exact ((T.restrictedObject W).obj.thickening.ideal_eq_ker U).symm

/-- On an affine open `U` of `V`, the divided power ideal of the restriction `(X, Y, γ)|_V` is
generated by the image of the divided power ideal of `S`. -/
theorem ideal_map_restrictedObject (U : (T.liftingOpen W).toScheme.affineOpens) :
    Ideal.map (((T.liftingOpen W).toScheme.presheaf.map
        (homOfLE (show U.1 ≤ ⊤ from le_top)).op).hom.comp
          (T.restrictedObject W).obj.toBase.hom.appTop.hom) (S.S.ideal.obj (op ⊤)) =
      (T.restrictedObject W).obj.thickening.target.ideal.obj (op U.1) := by
  have := T.isAffine
  have := T.isSmooth
  have hring : ((T.liftingOpen W).toScheme.presheaf.map
      (homOfLE (show U.1 ≤ ⊤ from le_top)).op).hom.comp
        ((T.liftingOpen W).ι ≫ T.toBase).appTop.hom =
      (T.Y.presheaf.map (homOfLE (show (T.liftingOpen W).ι ''ᵁ U.1 ≤ ⊤ from le_top)).op).hom.comp
        T.toBase.appTop.hom := by
    have hc : ((T.liftingOpen W).ι ≫ T.toBase).appTop ≫
        (T.liftingOpen W).toScheme.presheaf.map (homOfLE (show U.1 ≤ ⊤ from le_top)).op =
          T.toBase.appTop ≫ T.Y.presheaf.map
            (homOfLE (show (T.liftingOpen W).ι ''ᵁ U.1 ≤ ⊤ from le_top)).op := by
      rw [Scheme.Hom.comp_appTop, Category.assoc]
      congr 1
      exact Scheme.Opens.ι_appLE _ ⊤ U.1 _
    exact congrArg CommRingCat.Hom.hom hc
  refine (congrArg (fun f => Ideal.map f (S.S.ideal.obj (op ⊤))) hring).trans ?_
  exact ideal_map_appTop_restrict S T.prime_nilpotent T.Y T.toBase T.toY T.cartesian
    ⟨(T.liftingOpen W).ι ''ᵁ U.1, U.2.image_of_isOpenImmersion _⟩

/-- On an affine open `U` of `V`, the divided power ideal of the object `(W, V, γ)` of the
restricted situation is generated by the image of the divided power ideal of `S`: it is the ideal
of `(X, Y, γ)|_V` there (`ideal_obj_extendedObject`), and the two structure morphisms to `S`
agree. -/
theorem ideal_map_extendedObject (U : (T.liftingOpen W).toScheme.affineOpens) :
    Ideal.map (((T.liftingOpen W).toScheme.presheaf.map
        (homOfLE (show U.1 ≤ ⊤ from le_top)).op).hom.comp
          (T.extendedObject W).obj.toBase.hom.appTop.hom) (S.S.ideal.obj (op ⊤)) =
      (T.extendedObject W).obj.thickening.target.ideal.obj (op U.1) := by
  rw [T.extendedObject_toBase_hom W, T.ideal_obj_extendedObject W U]
  exact T.ideal_map_restrictedObject W U

/-- **The identity of `V` is a morphism of divided power schemes from the ambient divided power
scheme of `(W, V, γ)` to that of `(X, Y, γ)|_V`.**  Both lie over `S` by the same morphism of
schemes `V ↪ Y ⟶ S`, and the ideal of the target is generated by the ideal of `S` on affine
opens (`ideal_map_restrictedObject`), so this is
`Crystalline.DividedPowerScheme.isDPMorphism_app_of_ideal_map`. -/
def targetHom :
    (T.extendedObject W).obj.thickening.target ⟶ (T.restrictedObject W).obj.thickening.target where
  hom := 𝟙 (T.liftingOpen W).toScheme
  compatible := DividedPowerScheme.isDPMorphism_app_of_ideal_map (T.restrictedObject W).obj.toBase
    (T.extendedObject W).obj.toBase (𝟙 (T.liftingOpen W).toScheme)
    ((Category.id_comp _).trans (T.extendedObject_toBase_hom W).symm)
    (T.ideal_map_restrictedObject W)

/-- **The identity of `V` is a morphism of divided power schemes from the ambient divided power
scheme of `(X, Y, γ)|_V` to that of `(W, V, γ)`**, by the same argument as `targetHom` with the
roles exchanged, using `ideal_map_extendedObject`. -/
def targetHomInv :
    (T.restrictedObject W).obj.thickening.target ⟶ (T.extendedObject W).obj.thickening.target where
  hom := 𝟙 (T.liftingOpen W).toScheme
  compatible := DividedPowerScheme.isDPMorphism_app_of_ideal_map (T.extendedObject W).obj.toBase
    (T.restrictedObject W).obj.toBase (𝟙 (T.liftingOpen W).toScheme)
    ((Category.id_comp _).trans (T.extendedObject_toBase_hom W))
    (T.ideal_map_extendedObject W)

/-- The underlying morphism of schemes of `targetHom` is the identity of `V`. -/
@[simp]
theorem targetHom_hom : (T.targetHom W).hom = 𝟙 (T.liftingOpen W).toScheme := rfl

/-- The underlying morphism of schemes of `targetHomInv` is the identity of `V`. -/
@[simp]
theorem targetHomInv_hom : (T.targetHomInv W).hom = 𝟙 (T.liftingOpen W).toScheme := rfl

/-- The morphism of `CRIS(X/S)` from `(W, V, γ)` to `(X, Y, γ)|_V`: the identification
`W ≅ X ×_Y V` on thickened schemes and the identity of `V` on ambient schemes. -/
def toRestrictedObject : (T.extendedObject W).obj ⟶ (T.restrictedObject W).obj where
  sourceHom := (T.sourceIso W).hom
  targetHom := T.targetHom W
  immersion_naturality := (Category.comp_id _).trans (T.restrictToY_eq W)
  base_naturality := DividedPowerScheme.Hom.ext <|
    (Category.id_comp _).trans (T.extendedObject_toBase_hom W).symm
  toX_naturality := by
    change (T.sourceIso W).hom ≫ (T.toY ⁻¹ᵁ T.liftingOpen W).ι ≫ 𝟙 S.X = 𝟙 W.toScheme ≫ W.ι
    simp [sourceIso]

/-- The morphism of `CRIS(X/S)` from `(X, Y, γ)|_V` to `(W, V, γ)`, inverse to
`toRestrictedObject`. -/
def ofRestrictedObject : (T.restrictedObject W).obj ⟶ (T.extendedObject W).obj where
  sourceHom := (T.sourceIso W).inv
  targetHom := T.targetHomInv W
  immersion_naturality := by
    change (T.toY ∣_ T.liftingOpen W) ≫ 𝟙 _ = (T.sourceIso W).inv ≫ T.restrictToY W
    rw [Category.comp_id, restrictToY_eq, Iso.inv_hom_id_assoc]
  base_naturality := DividedPowerScheme.Hom.ext <|
    (Category.id_comp _).trans (T.extendedObject_toBase_hom W)
  toX_naturality := by
    change (T.sourceIso W).inv ≫ 𝟙 W.toScheme ≫ W.ι = (T.toY ⁻¹ᵁ T.liftingOpen W).ι ≫ 𝟙 S.X
    simp [sourceIso]

/-- **The object of the restricted situation, carried to `CRIS(X/S)`, is the restriction of the
object of the whole situation to `V`**, in the big crystalline category. -/
def restrictToOpenThickeningIso : (T.extendedObject W).obj ≅ (T.restrictedObject W).obj where
  hom := T.toRestrictedObject W
  inv := T.ofRestrictedObject W
  hom_inv_id :=
    Thickening.Hom.ext (T.sourceIso W).hom_inv_id (DividedPowerScheme.Hom.ext (Category.id_comp _))
  inv_hom_id :=
    Thickening.Hom.ext (T.sourceIso W).inv_hom_id (DividedPowerScheme.Hom.ext (Category.id_comp _))

/-- **The object `(W, V, γ)` of the situation of [Stacks, Tag 07MW] restricted to an open `W` of
`X`, carried back to `Cris(X/S)` by change of base, is the restriction `(X, Y, γ)|_V` of the
object `(X, Y, γ)` of the whole situation to the open `V = h⁻¹(W)` of `Y`.**  On thickened schemes
the isomorphism is `W ≅ X ×_Y V`, on ambient schemes it is the identity of `V`; that the identity
of `V` respects the two divided power structures is the uniqueness of extensions of `γ`
(`targetHom`, `targetHomInv`). -/
def restrictToOpenCrystallineThickeningIso :
    (smallExtend S ⊤ W (le_sourceToBase_preimage_top W)).obj
        (T.restrictToOpen W).crystallineThickening ≅
      T.crystallineThickening.restrictOpen
        (CrystallineThickening.ambientToXPreimage T.crystallineThickening W) :=
  (CrystallineThickening.fullyFaithfulι S).preimageIso (T.restrictToOpenThickeningIso W)

/-- The underlying morphism of `CRIS(X/S)` of `restrictToOpenCrystallineThickeningIso` is
`toRestrictedObject`. -/
@[simp]
theorem restrictToOpenCrystallineThickeningIso_hom_hom :
    (T.restrictToOpenCrystallineThickeningIso W).hom.hom = T.toRestrictedObject W := rfl

/-- The underlying morphism of `CRIS(X/S)` of the inverse of
`restrictToOpenCrystallineThickeningIso` is `ofRestrictedObject`. -/
@[simp]
theorem restrictToOpenCrystallineThickeningIso_inv_hom :
    (T.restrictToOpenCrystallineThickeningIso W).inv.hom = T.ofRestrictedObject W := rfl

end Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite.Situation07MW

